How Cowork evaluates skills ?
  Cowork evaluates it automatically and returns a plain-language quality report. You don't need to ask for the evaluation.
  A skill can fail in two ways: it doesn't trigger when it should (or it takes requests meant for another skill), or it triggers and does the wrong thing. Evaluation is designed to catch both before you rely on the skill in daily work.
  The depth of evaluation scales with the skill's reach (personal, team, organization, or store) and its risk level (low, medium, or high).
  
  Cowork runs two kinds of checks:
  
  Static checks: review the skill's structure and limits, scan any bundled code for security issues, and check the skill's text for prompt-injection patterns. Code is never executed during static checks.
  Behavioral checks: run the skill against realistic prompts. Cowork evaluates the output, the actions the skill takes, and how efficiently it uses tools. Triggering is scored for precision and recall rather than as a single number.
  
  Cowork scores each skill from 0 to 100 across four dimensions worth 25 points each:
  
  Trigger clarity: the skill fires at the right time.
  Instruction specificity: the skill knows what to do.
  Scope boundaries: the skill stays within its intended purpose.
  Robustness: the skill handles unexpected input safely.


Build apps with the App skill (Frontier):

  The built-in App skill lets you create lightweight, interactive apps in Cowork without writing code. Cowork invokes the skill when you describe an app you want to build.
  Ask Cowork to add features, such as showing participant info as cards. The app updates instantly as you make changes.
  Your app saves automatically as you work. Publishing makes your app, and your latest changes, available to the users you share it with. After you publish, share the app with a link so anyone in your organization who can use Microsoft 365 Copilot can open and use it.

